As $AC$ and $BC$ are tangents, we get:
$$\begin{align*}
\angle CAB &= \angle CBA
\end{align*}$$
and so by part (i):
$$\begin{align*}
\angle EAP &= \angle FBP
\end{align*}$$
Hence $\triangle EAP \sim \triangle FBP$. From $\triangle EAP\sim\triangle FBP$, corresponding sides give $\frac{EP}{AP}=\frac{FP}{BP}$. From part (i), $\triangle APG\sim\triangle BPE$ gives $\frac{EP}{BP}=\frac{GP}{AP}$. Thus:
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{EP}{AP} &= \frac{FP}{BP} \\
\frac{EP}{PB} &= \frac{PG}{AP}
\end{align*}$$
Hence:
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{EP}{FP} &= \frac{AP}{BP} \\
\frac{AP}{BP} &= \frac{PG}{EP}
\end{align*}$$
Therefore:
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{EP}{FP} &= \frac{PG}{EP} \\
EP^2 &= FP \times GP
\end{align*}$$

